    "lawCode": "Amd §§3216, 3221 & 4303, Ins L; amd §§2404 & 2803-o, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7881\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law and the public health law, in relation\nto providing coverage and information on chest wall reconstruction\nsurgery after a mastectomy or partial mastectomy\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to ensure that women who select chest wall\nreconstruction surgery have the proper insurance coverage for the opera-\ntion.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the insurance law to include the coverage of chest wall\nreconstruction surgery, in addition to breast reconstruction surgery,\nafter a mastectomy or partial mastectomy. It includes aesthetic flat\nclosure, a type of chest wall reconstruction, as defined by the National\nCancer Institute. Additionally, subdivisions 1 and 1-a of section 2404\nof the public health law are amended so that chest wall reconstructive\ninformation is included in the summary written by the commissioner.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAbout 1 in 8 U.S. women (about 13%) will be diagnosed with invasive\nbreast cancer during their lifetimes. Many of these women undergo\nmastectomies or partial mastectomies as part of their treatment to\nremove their cancer. While many women pursue reconstructive surgeries,\nsome women also choose to \"stay flat\" and pursue aesthetic flat closure,\nrather than a breast reconstruction. This bill will protect women and\nensure satisfactory aesthetic outcomes; as agreed upon by the mastectomy\npatient and surgeon(s) should the patient decide to \"go flat.\" This bill\nwill ensure that this surgery is covered by insurance and that doctors\ndiscuss the option with their patient for informed consent.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
